{
  "requirement": "The `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents not to commit requirements or write implementation or test code until the user has agreed to, rejected, or deferred every group.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject has a single obligation. The `habeas-requirements` skill MUST direct agents not to commit requirements or write implementation or test code until the user has agreed to, rejected, or deferred every group.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[the_requirements_skill_gates_commit_and_code_on_every_group_being_decided]` carries the `{test}` reference. It calls `assert_phrases(\"habeas-requirements\", ...)` with the phrase \"**Gate:** no implementation or test code, and no commit, until the user has agreed to, rejected, or deferred every group\".\n\nThe helpers are `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[assert_phrases]`, `fn[assert_text]` and `fn[bundled_skill]`. `bundled_skill` collapses whitespace across `SKILL.md` and its reference files. `assert_text` uses `contains` and panics if the phrase is missing. The assertion therefore enforces the text.\n\nThe search showed the phrase in `assets/skills/habeas-requirements/SKILL.md`, in a workflow step with its line breaks collapsed, so the test would pass against it.\n\nThe phrase covers every element of the obligation:\n- both prohibited actions: no implementation or test code, and no commit;\n- all three outcomes: agreed, rejected and deferred;\n- the quantifier \"every group\".\n\nA skill that dropped the gate, left out the commit prohibition, or listed fewer outcomes would fail this test. For a requirement about what a skill document directs, a text-presence assertion is the appropriate check. The requirement has no other modes, boundaries or failure cases. No `{fixme}` is involved.",
